            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Paula"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a favorite of ours because it tastes great and is quick and easy to fix. I omit the oil to lessen the calories and add only 8 oz. of the smoked turkey sausage to the rice mix and water. My husband likes to top his with grated sharp cheddar."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tiffany Durham"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a great basic recipe. Yes, the box does most of the work. I recommend sautéing onion, bell pepper and celery first as an add in. You can also throw a can of tomatoes with green chiles in the mix for more texture and flavor! The sausage can be left out for a vegetarian dish or substituted with shrimp or chicken as well. Starting with Zatarains just makes the whole thing easier and starts with great flavors.",
            "datePublished": "2021-01-13T14:28:15.330Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Meg"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is super easy and tasty, though I almost gave it three stars because, as another reviewer said, Zatarains does all the work. I also made a few changes: I sautéed onions, celery and pepper, and I used about half the meat but added a cup or so of homemade beans. I made it in an instant pot.",
            "datePublished": "2019-07-28T03:24:35.403Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mrwidgeon1948"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I cut the turkey andouille into rounds then halves before browning them in a little olive oil. This makes more meat per bite and takes a little heat out of it for my wife. Then I add a can of low sodium small red beans I've heated in the microwave for about 4 minutes with a little water because we like more beans and pre-heating them makes them softer and less \"crunchy\". I season the water with a heaping teaspoon of bacon grease from a supply I keep in the fridge, this replaces the ham hocks that were originally used in RB's, you can't taste it and by the time the beans are done you don't notice it all, but it's there. I don't use the usual hot sauce, we like Trappey's hot vinegar sauce instead (something like that). It's clear and not as hot as the red stuff.",
            "datePublished": "2026-04-11T03:57:17.606Z"
          },
          {
